candidates.change:
At index build:
- store the volume serial, UsnJournalID, NextUsn, and a FRN->relpath map of the about 3300 corpus directories.
On each query:
- open the volume and read records since the stored USN (FSCTL_READ_USN_JOURNAL, or FSCTL_READ_UNPRIVILEGED_USN_JOURNAL);
- keep the records whose parent FRN is in the map;
- turn them into changed, added, deleted and renamed paths;
- stat only those, and feed them into the existing S4 overlay.
Fall back to the walk when any of these hold:
- the journal ID changed, or the first USN is beyond the stored one (the journal wrapped);
- the volume is not local NTFS/ReFS, or access is denied;
- the record count exceeds N;
- a new directory appears (then walk that subtree).
Files: new internal/code/freshness/usn_windows.go plus a stub _other.go, and the drift entry in query/load.go and query/grep.go.

Merge the graph fingerprint and the corpus Files map into one binary stamp table, sorted by path, with {size, mtime_ns, sha256} plus graph/corpus membership bits. Do one compare pass over the memoized walk that yields both the graph drift and the corpus drift.
At build time, persist next to it:
- the parsed ignore patterns, keyed by source stamp;
- the trackedDirs set;
- the SearchCorpus result, so it is recomputed only when the source stamps (git index, config, ignore files) differ.
Files: freshness/fingerprint.go, corpus/record.go, corpus/probe.go (rulesFromRecord, Compare), query/load.go, query/grep.go.

trigram/format.go:
- read the header and the gram table via ReadAt, or map the file (the zz_spike_mmap*.go work underway);
- read only the posting ranges for the query's grams;
- store the file table as an offset array, so only candidate ids are turned into strings.
corpus/record.go: store the Digest in the record at build time and compare stored vs stored, with no recompute.
Keep LAZYIDX's rule: any validation failure falls back to a scan, never to 'no candidates'.
